    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 62 tests pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the idempotent-create rule on `POST /api/owners` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Changes** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n1. **Store** \u2014 added a `ConcurrentHashMap<String, Integer> idempotentCreates` field mapping each seen `Idempotency-Key` header value to the id of the owner created under it.\n\n2. **Lookup at entry** \u2014 at the start of `addOwner`, if the request carries an already-seen key, it looks the original owner up and returns it with **200 OK** (no duplicate created, skipping the checks that would otherwise yield a 409).\n\n3. **Record after create** \u2014 after a successful `saveOwner`, the key is stored against the new owner's id, so only genuinely-created keys are remembered.\n\n4. **Header access** \u2014 since the generated `OwnersApi` interface fixes the method signature (no header parameter), I read `Idempotency-Key` from the bound request via `RequestContextHolder`/`ServletRequestAttributes`, treating absent/blank as \"no key.\"\n\nThe design keys off the header alone as the spec describes (\"a create that repeats with an already-seen key\"), and only remembers keys after a create actually succeeds, so a failed/rejected attempt doesn't poison the key.",
