    "probe_text": "The controller code confirms the traced flow exactly. Here is the complete, ordered list of everything applied when creating an owner via `POST /api/owners` (handler: `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`).\n\n## Before the controller body runs (framework)\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java:129`). Caller must have `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, else 403.\n2. **Bean Validation on the request body** \u2014 `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` on the `@Validated` `OwnersApi` interface. Constraints on the **DTO** fire here (and *only* these \u2014 the `Owner` entity's own constraints are never triggered):\n   - `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size(1,30)`\n   - `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,80)`\n   - `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1,20)`\n   - `email` \u2014 `@Size(1,255)`, `@Email`\n   - `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`\n   - `title`, `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size` bounds\n   - Failure \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400 via `ExceptionControllerAdvice`.\n\n   There are no custom validators or validation groups for owners.\n\n## Inside the controller body (in execution order)\n\n3. **Idempotency short-circuit** (`:135-144`) \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header matches a previously successful create, return that existing owner with **200 OK** (no new create).\n4. **Telephone normalization + validation** (`:145-148`) \u2014 `normalizeTelephone()` strips separators, applies `+61` default, enforces `+` then 8\u201315 digits and national-length rules. Invalid \u2192 **400**.\n5. **Disposable-email rejection** (`:149-151`) \u2014 blocks `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com` \u2192 **400**.\n6. **DTO \u2192 entity mapping** (`:152`) \u2014 MapStruct `toOwner`. *Side effect:* entity setters normalize as they run \u2014 address fields are trimmed/upper-cased with street-abbreviation expansion (ST\u2192STREET, etc.), and email is lower-cased.\n7. **Address presence check** (`:158-162`) \u2014 composed address (structured `addressLine1[+line2]` preferred, else flat `address`) must be non-blank \u2192 else **400**; the composed value is written back via `setAddress()`.\n8. **Apply normalized telephone** to entity (`:163`).\n9. **Postcode-vs-city validation** (`:164-166`) \u2014 for known cities (Sydney 2000\u20132099, Melbourne 3000\u20133099, Brisbane 4000\u20134099) the postcode must fall in range \u2192 else **400**.\n10. **Compute household id** (`:171`) \u2014 deterministic SHA-256 of `(lastName, postcode)`, set on the entity up front.\n11. **Read `sharesHousehold` flag** (`:172`).\n12. **Hard-duplicate / identity check** (`:177-182`) \u2014 loads **all** owners, ignores soft-deleted, rejects if any has an equal `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) \u2192 **409**.\n13. **Household-duplicate check** (`:188-191`) \u2014 if any non-deleted owner shares the computed household id and `sharesHousehold` is not true \u2192 **409**.\n14. **Per-city capacity cap** (`:192-194`) \u2014 \u2265 50 owners in that city \u2192 **409**.\n15. **Future registration-date guard** (`:195-197`) \u2014 supplied `registrationDate` after today \u2192 **400**.\n16. **Business-day roll** (`:198-200`) \u2014 `toBusinessDay()` advances the effective date past weekends and the fixed 2026 public-holiday set; defaults to today when none supplied.\n17. **Per-day create limit** (`:201-204`) \u2014 \u2265 100 owners registered on that date \u2192 **429**.\n18. **Bulk-signup warning flag** (`:205`) \u2014 set true when > 80 registered that day.\n19. **Derived fields set on the entity** (`:207-220`):\n    - `registrationDate` = rolled business day\n    - `customerCode` = `<region>-<HASH8>` (SHA-256 of telephone+lastName) with a uniqueness suffix scanning existing codes\n    - `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with the same name\n    - `bulkSignupWarning`\n    - `householdSize` = existing household members + 1\n    - `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 soft-match on same last name + postcode but different telephone (skipped when `sharesHousehold`)\n20. **Persist** (`:221`) \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)`; this service method is the `@Transactional` boundary and does nothing but `ownerRepository.save`. Insert is chosen because id is null (`@GeneratedValue IDENTITY`). **No JPA lifecycle callbacks, no entity listeners, no auditing.**\n21. **Record idempotency key** (`:222-224`) \u2014 store `key \u2192 owner.id` in the in-memory map.\n22. **Audit log** (`:225-227`) \u2014 write an `AUDIT` logger line with id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel, membershipNumber.\n23. **Build response** (`:228-231`) \u2014 map to `OwnerDto` (computes displayName/initials/selfLink), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, return **201 Created**.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- **No password encoding** and **no application events** occur in owner creation.\n- The `Owner` entity's own Bean Validation annotations (E.164 telephone `@Pattern`, `@Email`, `@NotEmpty`, etc.) are **never exercised** on this path \u2014 only the DTO constraints plus the hand-rolled controller checks run.\n- The controller's own rejections (400/409/429) are returned as plain `ResponseEntity`s and do **not** pass through the `@ControllerAdvice`.\n- Duplicate/count checks call `findAllOwners()` repeatedly, loading the whole owners table into memory on every create."
